  "description": "Add real-time, expressive avatars to your AI agents and applications. Explore resources, tutorials, API docs, and dynamic examples to get the most out of Keyframe Lab's developer platform.",
  "markdown": {
    "instructions": [
      "Keyframe Labs is the real-time rendering layer for AI: it takes streaming audio from any agent framework or speech-to-speech LLM and returns a photorealistic, lip-synced avatar as live video. It does not replace your agent, LLM, or voice stack; it sits on top of them.",
      "Terminology: the docs and UI say 'avatar', but API fields, SDK classes, and model names use 'persona' (persona_id, persona_slug, PersonaEmbed, PersonaView, persona-1.5-live). These identifiers are correct as-is; never rename them to 'avatar' in code.",
      "The current model is persona-1.5-live. Do not reference persona-1-live; it is retired.",
      "There are three integration paths: Widget (no-code, agent designed on the Keyframe platform), Hosted (bring your own agent or LLM, low-code PersonaEmbed), and Self managed (bring your own agent or LLM, keys stay on your infrastructure, custom embed via PersonaView). Read /guides/getting-started/choose-integration-path.md before recommending one.",
      "Documented integrations: LiveKit (plugin), ElevenLabs Agents and OpenAI Realtime (each available hosted or via WebSocket), and meetings (Zoom, Google Meet, Microsoft Teams). This list is not exhaustive.",
      "Custom agents and other frameworks are fully supported via the self-managed WebSocket approach: any stack that can stream audio can drive a Keyframe avatar. Follow the same recipe as the ElevenLabs Agents WebSocket and OpenAI Realtime WebSocket guides, swapping in your own audio source, and use only the Keyframe SDK (@keyframelabs/sdk) as the reference — it is the only package that supports custom agent bindings today. Do not use Keyframe Elements (PersonaEmbed/PersonaView) or the React bindings (@keyframelabs/react) for custom platforms; they only support the natively integrated agent types (ElevenLabs Agents, OpenAI Realtime, Keyframe Voice Agent). A dedicated 'Custom or other agents' guide is coming.",
      "API keys are created at https://platform.keyframelabs.com/api-keys, are shown only once, and must stay server-side. Only publishable keys for low-code components belong in client code."
    ]
  },
